% A software supply chain: 160 packages, 292 dependency edges, 12 of
% them services you actually deploy.  One package has a CVE.
%
%   python3 datalog.py -q 'exposed(S, C)' programs/supply-chain.dl
%   python3 datalog.py --explain 'exposed(pkg4, cve_2026_0001)' programs/supply-chain.dl
%
% Three rules.  The question they answer — which deployed services are
% reachable to the vulnerable package, through any depth of transitive
% dependency — cannot be read off the facts, and being 95%% right means
% shipping an unpatched service.
%
% Generated deterministically (layered graph, seed 0) so the answer is
% stable; benchmarks/generate.py makes larger ones.

